      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Following amputation of a lower extremity for osteogenic sarcoma, the lumbar muscles receive an asymmetric strain. This predisposes to low-back-pain. When this occurs, tumour-recurrence must be excluded. This report demonstrates the usefulness of high-resolution computed tomography (CT) in this clinical situation."},
